From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NP <50584693+NatePu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:18:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] T1.3: generation bump sites, learn gate, admission/bump trace

- 40 flow_gen_bump()/flow_gate_update() hooks in 16 files, each under
  #if NFLOW > 0 and after the change it reports (DESIGN 5.4): route add,
  delete, RTM_CHANGE (also partial failures), link-state walk, PMTU CAS
  and reset; ARP lladdr change and invalidation; if_linkstate, lladdr,
  MTU, rdomain, monitor xflag; address add/purge; bridge brport and
  trunk/aggr trport (incl. SIOCSTRUNK); vlan destroy/up/down/link/tag/
  parent/prio; bpf attach/detach; forwarding, redirect and multipath
  sysctls; pf start/stop/xcommit; IPsec policy add (and gate on delete).
- flow_gate_update(): forwarding == 1, no IPsec, pf stopped or skipping
  an interface; recomputed under a leaf mutex (ERRATA E86).
- DIAGNOSTIC trace ring of bumps and admissions: ddb show flowtrace and
  raw kstat flow:0:trace; flow_trace_admit() for the MD hit path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
